@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

#
# prima-materia — the penalty that is not borne by the one who incurred it
#
# One generalization, formed from three claims already standing in the graph
# and set beside one another for the first time. The reading of the Huangting
# neijing jing supplied the third and made the shape visible, because its
# transmission clause puts the sanction on people who have been dead for seven
# generations, which is as far out of reach as a consequence can be put.
#
# The counter-search required by SPEC §16 was carried over the whole compiled
# holding before the statement was written, and it is recorded as
# pmp:DisplacedPenaltyCounterSearch in examinations/searches.ttl. It did not
# confirm the statement that was going to be written. It falsified the second
# half of it from inside the holding, and the node below is the statement that
# survived: the displacement is real and common enough to name, and it does
# not by itself put the rule out of reach, because the holding contains
# transmissions that displaced the penalty and then made it checkable again.
# What those cases have in common is set out in the notes, because it is the
# useful part of the finding and not a caveat on it.
#

pmc:ThePenaltyLaidOnAnotherParty a pm:Generalizing ;
    rdfs:label "The penalty for the fault is laid on someone who did not commit it"@en, "Die Strafe für den Fehler wird dem auferlegt, der ihn nicht begangen hat"@de ;
    pm:generalizedStatement "Where a transmission states what a defective or improperly transmitted performance costs, the cost is in a substantial minority of cases laid not on the performer but on a third party: the family or lineage the rite is done for, the dead ascendants of the person transmitting, or a class of beings to whom a debt is owed. The displacement separates the person positioned to notice the fault from the party who bears its consequence, and it does so in the operative text and not in a later gloss. It does not by itself make the rule unexaminable. It removes the consequence from the reach of the one person certain to know that the fault occurred, which is a different and weaker thing, and the check is restored wherever the displaced consequence is given a direction and a term."@en ;
    pm:generalizedFrom pmc:HawaiianWelfarePresupposesExactChanting, pmc:ShangqingHuangtingMengjin, pmc:HeterodoxWorshipNeverClearsTheDebt ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    skos:note "The three witnesses displace to three different distances, and the range is the point. In the Hawaiian case a breath taken before the close of a phrase is ill-luck to the person or family the chant honours, who are alive and can be watched, so that only the attribution and not the observation is out of reach. In the Chinese transmission clause the affliction of a wrongly conducted handing on is reported to the three palaces and falls on seven generations of ancestors, who cannot be examined at all and cannot be reported unafflicted. In the Sanskrit case the debt to ancestors, sages, gods and the human race is simply never cleared, and the price is paid in repeated rebirth, which places the consequence outside the life in which the fault was committed."@en ;
    skos:note "What the counter-search established about proportion should be kept with the claim, because it is the reason the statement says a substantial minority and not a rule. Of the forty stated consequences of a skipped prerequisite in the holding, four displace outright; of some fifty cautions, nine to eleven do. The commoner form by a wide margin is the penalty that falls on the practitioner's own body, memory, standing or attainment, and where that form is used the tradition can in principle be contradicted from inside, as one of the holding's own nodes says of itself."@en ;
    skos:note "The witnesses also cluster rather than distribute, and a reader should not take this for a cross-traditional regularity. Two corpora carry the displacement as their normal form: the burial literature, in which a badly sited or badly dated grave cuts off the sons and kills the grandsons, and the needling canon, in which the operator's error is paid for by the patient within a stated number of days. Outside those two the instances are scattered, and the three witnesses above were chosen from three unconnected transmissions in order not to rest the statement on either cluster."@en ;
    skos:note "The second half of an earlier draft of this statement said that the displacement puts the rule beyond checking, and the counter-search killed it. Three kinds of case in the holding refuse it. A purification performed by the unqualified is said to make the sickness and death in the world stronger than they were, which is a directional claim about a countable thing and therefore decidable in a way that mere failure is not. A burial doctrine that placed its effects a generation away could never be caught, but one line of it fixes a class of effects within a day of a burial, and burials are public and dated; a seventh-century memorial accordingly set a count of more than twenty recorded burials against it. And a felling prohibition names the man who will die, sets ten days, and denies the obvious natural explanation in advance. What all three have that the three witnesses lack is a direction and a term. That is the condition under which a displaced consequence comes back within reach, and it is stated here as a finding and not as a hope."@en ;
    skos:note "Two further cases bear on the first half rather than the second and are worth naming so that the claim is not read too strongly. In one tradition the audience at the public night ceremony knows the songs well enough to catch a deviation, so the fault is reported by people other than the performer even though the displaced ill-luck is not; and in another the displaced consequence is reported by the transmission itself as having been seen to arrive, in two anecdotes that the defending commentary supplies and that were never traced to the works they name. The first shows that displacement of the consequence does not entail displacement of the observation of the fault. The second shows what an unfalsifiable displaced claim looks like when the tradition does try to confirm it."@en ;
    skos:note "Falsified by a count. If a survey of the operative transmission clauses across the holding's corpora found the displaced form to be the majority rather than the minority, the statement would have understated the shape and should be rewritten as a rule; if it found the displaced form confined to the two clusters named above and absent everywhere else, the statement would have overstated it and should be withdrawn to a remark about two corpora. Falsified in the other direction by an operative text that lays the penalty on a third party and in the same clause gives the performer a means of confirming that it arrived, without a direction or a term: that would break the condition the fourth note states."@en ;
    skos:note "The consequence for how such material is read is small and exact. A rule whose penalty is displaced cannot be tested by asking the practitioner whether it came true, because he is not the one it would come true to, and the absence of a report of the harm is not evidence that the harm did not occur. Anyone building a protocol on a transmission of this kind has to find the bearer before he can find the outcome, and in the case of the dead ascendants there is no bearer to find. That is a statement about what can be examined and not about what is the case."@en .
